diff --git a/ROADMAP.md b/ROADMAP.md
index 798d448..9547aa7 100644
--- a/ROADMAP.md
+++ b/ROADMAP.md
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ before redoing any of them; a zip without `.git` cannot tell.
 - **Talk T9, pointer input on the Talk screen (2026-11-15, docs/TALK.md 6k):** add-only `input_set_pointer` / `input_pointer` / `input_pointer_click` (`input.h`, `DOOMO_POINTER` 0 on GBA, PS1 and Dreamcast so they link none of it); on the Talk screen a click is exactly the matching pad press (quick reply, category, act, topic, typed line, Options, invite row, goodbye, a name in the people strip, the header = B, the scroll bar = L / R); a small arrow is drawn only while a pointer is present. Runner `mouse X Y [click]`, `expect-ptr-page`, `expect-ptr-row`; script `talk_pointer.txt`, `test_talk_pointer.c`. Not done: clicking the dialogue box, a wheel.
 - **Creator CR-BODY, body types and better sliders (2026-11-13; docs/CREATOR.md "CR-BODY", GBA ledger row 49, docs/PS1.md "CR-BODY"):** 6 new body types (gene `body` 10..15: Athletic, Gangly, Bean, Brick, Willowy, Bobble) as table rows (no new painter), one table for every slider's range (`CR_SLIDERS`, ready for the x1..x4 cheat of CR-SLIDERX), A resets a slider (own undo step), the bar shows the distance from the default, the horn size without horns and the turkey's six face sliders (they changed nothing) are not offered, and the test that moves EVERY build slider across its range (`test_cr_body.c`: each slider on every species and body, every step on the bench, canary bytes; `creator_sliders.txt` + `tools/slider_shots_check.py` on the native runner, GBA `make -C gba test-creator-sliders`, PS1 harness and Dreamcast `ui-compare`). PS1 `_end` -16 B (72,336 B below the stack top on the landed tree; the 72 KB gate is 1,392 B short, inherited from the tip), GBA EWRAM / IWRAM identical, ROM +2.9 KB; Head size repeats its last steps on the stepped bodies (Bobble 4 of 16; pinned by a test); old saves and Classic premades unchanged. Left for CR-SLIDERX: the cheat itself.
 - **Creator CR4 batch A5, outfit (2026-11-13; docs/CREATOR.md "CR4 batch A5"):** 70 new parts live, the gene-stored part of the batch: 24 tops (gene `top` 25..48), 31 outer layers (`outer` 1..31) and 15 legwear (`legwear` 1..15; the outer layer and legwear lists were empty, so the Outfit tab gets those rows for the first time), hand-written part scripts in `core/data/parts/outfit` and the new `wardrobe`, shape gate (the gene-only lists have their own in `test_cr4_a5.c`), cost weights, frozen ids, review line A5, contact sheets incl. the new `portrait_sheet --interplay-outfit` (outer layers x tops x backpieces), runner walk-through `creator_parts_outfit.txt`. Old saves, premades and Classic islands unchanged. Not in A5: gene-stored tops 49..63 (15), bottoms (20), shoes (20) and prints (24), and the deep fields (tops / outer / bottoms / legwear / shoes page 2, socks, fabric tiles: need CR5).
+- **UI-OPTIONS (built 2026-11-15, the UI stream; `docs/design/UI_PLAN.md` 4.1, `docs/GBA.md` "UI-OPTIONS: the Options screen rebuilt", ledger row UI-OPTIONS, `docs/PS1.md`, `docs/DREAMCAST.md`):** Options rebuilt: nine tabs in one strip (Quick, Game, Life, Display, Sound, Controls, Access, Perf, Cheats: the open one by name, the rest as icons), group headers, at most 12 rows a page, a row counter in the header, one help line per row (at most 36 letters, in English and Spanish), a detail card behind SELECT (X on a Dreamcast pad) for the long texts, Y puts one row back to its default (never Language or Monster Mode), a gold dot on a changed row, previews (Crosshair, Field of view, Text speed, Clock, HUD layout), a blip on the volume sliders, one hint bar of three actions, and Options opens on the page it was left on. Option ids, OPT / OPT2 and the preset / reset rules unchanged (old saves load). GBA `speed2_options`: every window 30.0 fps with every frame 2 vblanks, work 24.4-26.2 ms a tick (old screen 23.7-26.5); the backdrop leaves out what the window covers (exact: every page's screenshot byte for byte). EWRAM -72 B, IWRAM 0, PS1 110,608 B below the stack top (unchanged). Tests: `core/tests/test_ui_options.c` (every option on exactly one page, at most 12 rows a page, every help one line at both sizes in every ready language, defaults load, old ids keep their meaning, cursor / Y / card / page memory). **Still open:** the closed tabs show icons only, the kept panel for the rows (not needed for 30 here), PS1 / Dreamcast emulator runs and the UI-FIT tool (not on the branch yet).
 - **Done, CR4 A1b (the second face batch, docs/CREATOR.md "CR4 A1b"):** 51 new creator parts live: 12 noses (nose 12..23), 12 mouths (20..31), 16 ears (16..31), 11 blush styles (5..15) (part scripts `core/data/parts/face/a1b_*.txt`, review lines `A1b`, contact sheets viewed, `test_cr4_a1b.c`, `creator_parts_face_b.txt` runner walk-through); script material `mat blush`; small per-slot shape gates for nose / mouth / blush. Core tests 1,337 passed (also SAN=1), check-gen, xcheck, `make -C gba test` and `test-creator`, `dc-host-test`; GBA `.bss` / IWRAM identical (EWRAM net zero), PS1 `_end` 0x801ee550 before and after on the earlier tip (+0 B), 0x801df9f0 on the landing tip (132,624 B below the stack top); Re-verified on the landing tip (after CR5-FIX and TD1) (core, SAN=1, check-gen, xcheck, GBA test + test-creator, PS1 72,368 B, dc-host-test, PS1 harness all PASS). PS1 harness `game_smoke`, `creator_speed` (idle 30.13, rows 30.13, value 29.88), `creator_grid` and `creator_parts_face_b` PASS. Left: muzzles, teeth, freckles, scars (deep fields, CR5 is not on origin yet) and extra eyes 4-6 (gene change). Ear folds were already live.
 - **Creator CR-SLIDERX, the cheat "Slider range x1 / x2 / x3 / x4" (2026-11-15; docs/CREATOR.md "CR-SLIDERX", GBA ledger row 58, docs/PS1.md "CR-SLIDERX"):** Options > Cheats, OPT2 id 69 (`OPT_SLIDER_RANGE`; an old save reads x1; ungated). It multiplies the effect and the range of the 11 build sliders through the CR-BODY slider table: the drawn look of a grown-up goes `def + (value - def) * m`, clamped to each slider's measured safe range (`look_sliders[]`, -14..29 for Height ... -2..27 for Nose and Mouth); the saved sliders stay 0..15, so a look made at x3 is the same look at x1 (nothing to clamp or flag, no save change); minors are never scaled; x1 is bit for bit what was drawn before. The 11 `DoomoLook` fields are `int8_t`. The creator preview and the bar value ("+9" at x3) follow. Tests: `test_cr_sliderx.c` (12; every slider x every multiplier x every step on bust, figure, fighter and chibi: changes exactly when the effective value changes, canary bytes, every species and body; the cache x1 -> x3 -> x1; the OPT2 round trip) and the walk-through at x2, x3, x4 (`creator_sliders_x2/x3/x4.txt`, generated by `tools/slider_scripts.py`) on the runner, GBA `make -C gba test-creator-sliders`, the PS1 harness and the Dreamcast `ui-compare`. PS1 `_end` +256 B (72,336 -> 72,080 B below the stack top); GBA `.bss`/`.iwram`/`.iwram_bss`/`.data` identical (free EWRAM 12,164 B), ROM `.text` +192 B, `.rodata` +572 B.
 - **Creator CR4 batch A3, spooky (2026-11-13; docs/CREATOR.md "CR4 batch A3"):** 60 new parts live: 10 horns (gene `horns` 16..25), 16 tails (`tail` 16..31), 14 wings (`wings` 10..23), 4 halos (`halo` 12..15) and 16 auras (`aura` 8..23), hand-written part scripts in `core/data/parts/spooky` (no new painter code), shape gate, cost weights, frozen ids, review line A3, contact sheets incl. the new `portrait_sheet --slot tail|wings --views` (figure and the fighter's five views), runner walk-through `creator_parts_spooky.txt`, `test_cr4_a3.c`. Old saves, premades and Classic islands unchanged. Not in A3 (deep fields, need CR5): horn page 2 (6), horn / antenna bits (32), tail accessories (16), wing accessories (8), halo page 2 (6) = 68 of the batch's 134 (the other 6 are the painted halos live since CR3).
